            0.7,
            0.046,
            0.862,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "A Story of Numbers"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.328,
            0.121,
            0.421,
            0.164
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.496,
            0.096,
            0.797,
            0.197
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.218,
            0.848,
            0.274
          ],
          "content": "Thus, we have a new number system where each landmark number is 5 times the previous one. Since 1 is the first landmark number, they are all powers of 5."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.212,
            0.281,
            0.26,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": "5 ^ { 0 }   = 1",
          "image_source": "images/page_15_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.313,
            0.282,
            0.361,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": "5 ^ { 1 }   =   5",
          "image_source": "images/page_15_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.413,
            0.282,
            0.469,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": "5 ^ { 2 }   = 2 5",
          "image_source": "images/page_15_equation_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.512,
            0.282,
            0.579,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": "5 ^ { 3 }   = 1 2 5",
          "image_source": "images/page_15_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.621,
            0.282,
            0.687,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": "5 ^ { 4 }   = 6 2 5",
          "image_source": "images/page_15_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.73,
            0.282,
            0.805,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": "5 ^ { 5 }   = 3 1 2 5",
          "image_source": "images/page_15_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.214,
            0.309,
            0.26,
            0.339
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.414,
            0.308,
            0.457,
            0.341
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.516,
            0.306,
            0.565,
            0.34
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.621,
            0.315,
            0.683,
            0.331
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.355,
            0.582,
            0.376
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "？ Express the number 143 in this new system."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.379,
            0.847,
            0.418
          ],
          "content": "Let us start grouping, starting with the size $5 ^ { 3 }   =   1 2 5$ , as this is the largest landmark number smaller than 143. We get—"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.348,
            0.422,
            0.649,
            0.44
          ],
          "content": "143 = 125 + 5 + 5 + 5 + 1 + 1 + 1.",
          "image_source": "images/page_15_equation_19.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.445,
            0.76,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": "So the number 143 in the new system is $\\textcircled{O}  \\square \\square \\square \\square \\triangle \\triangle \\triangle \\cdot$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.471,
            0.712,
            0.492
          ],
          "content": "Number systems having landmark numbers in which the"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.496,
            0.57,
            0.515
          ],
          "content": "(a) first landmark number is 1, and"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.52,
            0.847,
            0.576
          ],
          "content": "(b) every next landmark number is obtained by multiplying the current landmark number by some fixed number n is said to be a **base-n** number system."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.576,
            0.848,
            0.633
          ],
          "content": "The Egyptian number system is a base-10 system, and the number system that we created is a base-5 system. A base-10 number system is also called a **decimal number system.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.642,
            0.293,
            0.664
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.667,
            0.847,
            0.706
          ],
          "content": "1. Write the following numbers in the above base-5 system using the symbols in Table 2: 15, 50, 137, 293, 651."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.716,
            0.847,
            0.754
          ],
          "content": "2. Is there a number that cannot be represented in our base-5 system above? Why or why not?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.764,
            0.848,
            0.802
          ],
          "content": "3. Compute the landmark numbers of a base-7 system. In general, what are the landmark numbers of a base-n system?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.806,
            0.848,
            0.845
          ],
          "content": "The landmark numbers of a base-n number system are the powers of n starting from $n ^ { 0 } = 1 , n , n ^ { 2 } , n ^ { 3 } ,$ ..."
        },
        {
